---
// The two hashes that tie a request to the key: cnf.jkt (token → key) and ath (proof → token).
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 344" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="dp-bi-t dp-bi-d">
  <title id="dp-bi-t">How the token and the proof are bound to each other and to the key</title>
  <desc id="dp-bi-d">
    Left, the access token, which carries cnf.jkt, the thumbprint of the client's public key that the
    authorization server recorded. Right, the DPoP proof, which carries the public key as jwk and ath,
    the hash of the access token. The API runs two checks. One: the SHA-256 thumbprint of the proof's
    jwk must equal the token's cnf.jkt, so the proof was signed by the key the token was issued to.
    Two: the SHA-256 of the token must equal the proof's ath, so the proof was made for this token.
  </desc>

  <text x="4" y="20" font-size="17" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-store)">access token</text>
  <rect x="4" y="30" width="182" height="112" rx="6" stroke-width="1.5" style="fill: var(--viz-store-soft); stroke: var(--viz-store)" />
  <text x="14" y="56" font-size="15" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">sub: user-42</text>
  <text x="14" y="80" font-size="15" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">exp: +5 min</text>
  <text x="14" y="108" font-size="15" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">cnf.jkt:</text>
  <text x="14" y="130" font-size="15" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">0ZcOCOR…</text>

  <text x="214" y="20" font-size="17" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-flow)">DPoP proof</text>
  <rect x="214" y="30" width="182" height="112" rx="6" stroke-width="1.5" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
  <text x="224" y="56" font-size="15" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">jwk: {"{"} x, y {"}"}</text>
  <text x="224" y="80" font-size="15" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">htm, htu, iat</text>
  <text x="224" y="108" font-size="15" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">ath:</text>
  <text x="224" y="130" font-size="15" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">fUHyO2r…</text>

  <text x="4" y="176" font-size="16" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">The API recomputes both</text>

  <rect x="4" y="188" width="392" height="66" rx="8" stroke-width="1.5" style="fill: var(--viz-ok-soft); stroke: var(--viz-ok)" />
  <text x="16" y="214" font-size="16" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">
    <tspan>1. thumbprint(</tspan><tspan style="fill: var(--viz-flow)">jwk</tspan><tspan>) = </tspan><tspan style="fill: var(--viz-store)">cnf.jkt</tspan>
  </text>
  <text x="16" y="240" font-size="15" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">signed by the key the token was issued to</text>

  <rect x="4" y="266" width="392" height="66" rx="8" stroke-width="1.5" style="fill: var(--viz-ok-soft); stroke: var(--viz-ok)" />
  <text x="16" y="292" font-size="16" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">
    <tspan>2. SHA-256(</tspan><tspan style="fill: var(--viz-store)">token</tspan><tspan>) = </tspan><tspan style="fill: var(--viz-flow)">ath</tspan>
  </text>
  <text x="16" y="318" font-size="15" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">made for this token, not another one</text>
</svg>
